-- title:
--   Fppf covering sieves of affine schemes admit finite affine refinements
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring (an object of `CommRingCat` in universe $u$) and let $S$ be a sieve on the scheme $\operatorname{Spec} R$ which belongs to `Scheme.fppfTopology (Spec R)`, i.e. $S$ is a covering sieve for the Grothendieck topology generated by the fppf precoverage on schemes — the precoverage whose covering families are the jointly surjective families of morphisms that are flat and locally of finite presentation. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $\iota$ in universe $u$, a proof that $\iota$ is finite, a family of commutative rings $A_i$ indexed by $\iota$, and ring homomorphisms $\varphi_i \colon R \to A_i$, such that two things hold: first, the presieve generated by the arrows $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi_i \colon \operatorname{Spec} A_i \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ (in the sense of `Presieve.ofArrows`) lies in `Scheme.fppfPrecoverage (Spec R)`, so that the family is jointly surjective with every member flat and locally of finite presentation; and second, every arrow $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi_i$ is a member of the sieve $S$. Thus every fppf covering sieve of an affine scheme contains a finite fppf covering family consisting of morphisms of affine schemes.
--
--   This is the standard statement that an fppf covering of an affine scheme is refined by a finite fppf covering by affine schemes, here in the form that a covering sieve of the generated topology contains such a family. It is used in the descent-theoretic input to the argument, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_section_of_fppfAmitsurTrivial`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_section_of_fppfAmitsurTrivial).
